# The sift.test_* settings the release library defines although they are testing settings (scripts/check-test-settings.sh fails for any other one defined outside SIFT_TESTING).
# NAME, a tab, the reason. A regress test that sets only these runs on the release library too (scripts/check-testing-regress.sh).
sift.test_col_unit_rows	the rows a key-cut unit aims at: the regression tests that release-library-regress runs reach several units of a small table through it (agg_group_expr_sparse, agg_preagg_exceptions, col_merge_levels, col_overlay_cap, col_overlay_lean, col_overlay_merge, col_search, col_topn, col_zone_keep, facet_counts, tbl_topn); without it they would leave the release library's merge, overlay and zone paths unrun
sift.test_search_chunk_sbs	the superblocks whose BM25 matches an aggregate scan holds at a time, a tunable of the shipped scan (docs/COL-SEARCH.md names it): col_search, col_topn, facet_counts and tbl_topn run on the release library with a small value
